SAFETY AND RECOVERY FOR REMOTE LLM AGENTS

READ-ONLY FIRST
  help COMMAND, ps, pins, pwmctl status, cat /proc/memory,
  grep TEXT /proc/sym/kernel, bounded hexdump FILE OFFSET COUNT.

COMMANDS THAT CAN CHANGE STATE
  write_file, rm, kill, dd with of=..., echo > file,
  i2cctl write/xfer, pwmctl freq/a/b/off, framebuffer control,
  server startup/shutdown, raw memory access.
Ask the user before irreversible or hardware-affecting changes.

DO NOT EXECUTE THROUGH MCP
  bare python, edit, vi, fd, mem, gpio, fbed, pong, reversi, tictactoe, maze, mb,
  watch, trace follow, interactive omikuji -i, indefinite tcpdump,
  raw cat on infinite /dev nodes, long-running network listeners.

RECOVER FROM A FAILED CALL
  1) identify if the tool returned a normal result or transport
     failure (HTTP reset/incomplete chunked read);
  2) reopen MCP connection if needed;
  3) check ps, lsof and state without changing it;
  4) retry only idempotent, bounded read commands;
  5) warn the user before repeating a non-idempotent action.

WHEN OUTPUT IS TOO BIG
  hexdump FILE OFFSET 64
  trace show PID
  grep substring /man/PAGE
  get_manual(topic) one page rather than every page
If a single /man page exceeds the MCP output cap, use cat/grep
with a bounded transfer strategy; prefer keeping pages small.

REPORT RESULTS PRECISELY
  command issued, output received, exit/result when known,
  observed side effect, what remains unverified.
Avoid declaring success solely because a tool did not raise error.
